16 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Six charts with sequencing data analysis from gd T cells. Chart A shows total TRD molecule count for the three standard groups as a bar graph. Chart B and C are box plots that display the ratio between clonotypes and TRD molecules by group and by response in cutaneous melanoma patients, respectively.  Chart B shows a higher ratio for the cutaneous melanoma group, while for chart C the higher ratio belongs to the non-responders group, both compared with the control. Chart D shows top clonal proportions within groups. Chart E and F detail the frequency of Vd1, Vd2 and other clones per total number of cells, compared between groups, and between responders and non-responders, respectively. Chart E shows a significantly higher frequency in other clones from cutaneous melanoma compared with uveal melanoma.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows three treemaps, reflecting the clonotypes in the three groups, where no particular clonotype dominates. The clonotypes are color-coded by all the detected combinations of TRDV and TRDJ genes, and the colors belonging to TRDV1 and TRDV2 are more prevalent. Panels B, C, and D display heatmaps for repertoire overlap in cutaneous melanoma samples, control, and uveal melanoma samples, respectively. Overlap values are color-coded, with a scale from zero to four, the vast majority of overlap values being 0.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
